<title>USA: Clinton wants AMR, pilots to reach accord.</title>
<headline>Clinton wants AMR, pilots to reach accord.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Bill Clinton remains convinced that AMR Corp and its pilots should use federal mediation to resolve their dispute, White House spokesman Mike McCurry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;He (Clinton) remains convinced that the parties should and must use the available mediation board process to address their grievances and settle their disputes,&quot; McCurry said.</p>
<p>&quot;We are putting all energy and focus on the work the mediation board is doing and we remain in close contact with the chair of the mediation board,&quot; he said. &quot;I am not going to speculate at all about what happens if there's no agreement.&quot;</p>
</text>
